  "reason": "Evidence: config_039 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieved the best accuracy at 0.7250, and all top-5 results share multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted/concat fusion with scvi_n200. The only untested configuration that pairs the four best-validated settings (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) with an alternative RNA encoder is config_041 (pca_n2000). This experiment directly tests whether a simpler linear RNA representation can match or exceed the deep scvi_n200 encoder in the otherwise-optimal pipeline. As the final experiment, it provides a clean ablation (only RNA encoder differs from config_039), confirming whether scvi_n200's ~0.20 accuracy advantage over scgpt is specific to learned representations or generalizable to any non-trivial RNA encoding. This is the highest-value remaining test because it either discovers a competitive alternative or definitively closes the search by validating the best configuration found."
}

